# Ollama-OpenAI Proxy Project Architecture

This is the main **Ollama-OpenAI Proxy** project - a Go 1.25 application that provides OpenAI-compatible API for local Ollama models.

## 🏗️ Project Structure

### Entry Points
- [cmd/server/main.go](mdc:cmd/server/main.go) - HTTP server with OpenAI API endpoints
- [cmd/tui/main.go](mdc:cmd/tui/main.go) - Terminal UI for monitoring and management

### Core Configuration  
- [internal/config/config.go](mdc:internal/config/config.go) - Complete configuration system
- [configs/dev.yaml](mdc:configs/dev.yaml) - Development configuration
- [configs/production.yaml.example](mdc:configs/production.yaml.example) - Production template

### Architecture Layers
```
Client Apps (OpenAI API) → Proxy Server → Ollama Server
                            ↓
                    [API Keys & Auth] → [Models & Metrics]
                            ↓
                    [Terminal UI (TUI)]
```

## 🎯 Key Principles

### Go 1.25 Features
- Utilize **enhanced generics** where appropriate
- Use **improved WaitGroups** with proper error handling  
- Leverage **new vet analyzers** (`-waitgroup`, `-hostport`)
- Apply **memory leak detection** capabilities

### OpenAI Compatibility 
- **Exact API format** matching for `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/models`
- **Request/Response conversion** between OpenAI ↔ Ollama formats
- **Streaming support** for real-time responses
- **Error format consistency** with OpenAI standards

### Security First
- **API Key Management** with model-based access control
- **Rate Limiting** per API key with configurable limits
- **Audit Logging** for all authentication events
- **Secure storage** with bcrypt/argon2 hashing

### 100% Test Coverage
- Every component must have **comprehensive unit tests**
- **Integration tests** with mock Ollama server
- **Edge cases coverage** for all error scenarios
- **Performance benchmarks** for critical paths

